## Phase 3 instructions

1. Build all three candidates as `models/<A>/predict.py`,
   `models/<B>/predict.py`, `models/<C>/predict.py`.
2. Each needs a `notes.md` declaring its rung, parent, and expected
   residual character — and the mandatory `## What this differs from`
   section the iterate skill checks for.
3. Run `skills/iterate` on each. The gate determines which (if any) goes
   to `final-model/`.
4. If a per-platform bias term is fitted in any candidate, the fit step
   MUST use route-grouped CV and write `route_cv_sigma` into
   `coeffs.json`. The bias_without_route_cv gate refuses to ship
   otherwise (m4-cohort-findings.md §6 + §9).
5. If all three lose to V1 on dev CV, ship V1 with REPORT.md documenting
   why — but you should not be in that situation after three candidates
   from three different angles.

